+{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JDDPVq3uW55Bt8MnAZcdhx","type":"tool_result","content":"# Phase 1: Basic FIFO Queue\n\nImplement a `TaskQueue` class with the following interface:\n\n## Methods\n\n- **`enqueue(payload)`** - Add a task to the queue. Returns the created task object.\n- **`dequeue()`** - Remove and return the next task in FIFO order. Returns `null` if the queue is empty. Sets the task status to `processing`.\n- **`size()`** - Return the number of pending tasks in the queue.\n\n## Task Object\n\nEach task has the following properties:\n\n| Property    | Type     | Description                                    |\n|-------------|----------|------------------------------------------------|\n| `id`        | `string` | Auto-generated unique identifier (UUID format) |\n| `payload`   | `any`    | The data associated with the task              |\n| `status`    | `string` | One of: `pending`, `processing`, `completed`, `failed` |\n| `createdAt` | `Date`   | Timestamp when the task was created            |\n\n## Requirements\n\n- Tasks are returned in the order they were added (First-In, First-Out)\n- Each task gets a unique `id` automatically assigned\n- New tasks start with `status: 'pending'`\n- When dequeued, task status changes to `'processing'`\n- `dequeue()` returns `null` when the queue is empty\n\n## Export\n\nExport the `TaskQueue` class as a named export from `src/index.ts`.\n# Phase 2: Named Queues\n\nExtend the `TaskQueue` to support multiple named queues.\n\n## Updated Methods\n\n- **`enqueue(queueName, payload)`** - Add a task to a specific named queue. Returns the created task.\n- **`dequeue(queueName)`** - Get the next task from a specific named queue. Returns `null` if queue is empty or doesn't exist.\n- **`listQueues()`** - Return an array of all queue names that have been created.\n- **`queueSize(queueName)`** - Return the number of pending tasks in a specific queue.\n\n## Requirements\n\n- Each named queue operates independently\n- Enqueueing to a queue that doesn't exist creates it\n- Dequeueing from a non-existent queue returns `null`\n- If no queue name is specified, use `'default'` as the queue name\n- `listQueues()` returns names of all queues that have been created\n- Queue-specific sizes are tracked independently\n\n## Backward Compatibility\n\nThe single-argument `enqueue(payload)` should still work by using the `'default'` queue.\nSimilarly, `dequeue()` with no arguments should dequeue from `'default'`.\n# Phase 3: Priority\n\nAdd priority support to tasks.\n\n## Updated Methods\n\n- **`enqueue(queueName, payload, options?)`** - The options object can include `priority`.\n  - `priority`: number from 1 (highest) to 10 (lowest). Default is 5.\n\n## Requirements\n\n- `dequeue()` returns the highest priority task first (lowest number = highest priority)\n- Within the same priority level, FIFO order is preserved\n- Default priority is 5 if not specified\n- Priority values outside 1-10 should throw an error\n- Priority is per-queue (each named queue has its own priority ordering)\n- The task object should include a `priority` property\n# Phase 4: Delayed/Scheduled Tasks\n\nAdd support for delayed and scheduled task execution.\n\n## Updated Methods\n\n- **`enqueue(queueName, payload, options?)`** - Options can now include:\n  - `delay`: number of milliseconds before the task becomes available\n  - `runAt`: a `Date` object specifying when the task should become available\n  - (existing) `priority`: priority level\n\n## Requirements\n\n- A delayed task is enqueued immediately but not returned by `dequeue()` until the delay has elapsed\n- A `runAt` task becomes available at the specified time\n- Non-delayed tasks should be dequeued before delayed tasks that haven't become available yet\n- When multiple delayed tasks are available, they are ordered by their availability time (earliest first), then by priority, then FIFO\n- `delay` and `runAt` work with named queues\n- The task object should include a `availableAt` property (Date) indicating when the task becomes available","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"73578245-3916-44ab-a99c-085e0622a3f4","uuid":"9a77a42c-6785-4013-a844-923aea07304b","timestamp":"2026-07-25T15:49:08.564Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Phase 1: Basic FIFO Queue\n\nImplement a `TaskQueue` class with the following interface:\n\n## Methods\n\n- **`enqueue(payload)`** - Add a task to the queue. Returns the created task object.\n- **`dequeue()`** - Remove and return the next task in FIFO order. Returns `null` if the queue is empty. Sets the task status to `processing`.\n- **`size()`** - Return the number of pending tasks in the queue.\n\n## Task Object\n\nEach task has the following properties:\n\n| Property    | Type     | Description                                    |\n|-------------|----------|------------------------------------------------|\n| `id`        | `string` | Auto-generated unique identifier (UUID format) |\n| `payload`   | `any`    | The data associated with the task              |\n| `status`    | `string` | One of: `pending`, `processing`, `completed`, `failed` |\n| `createdAt` | `Date`   | Timestamp when the task was created            |\n\n## Requirements\n\n- Tasks are returned in the order they were added (First-In, First-Out)\n- Each task gets a unique `id` automatically assigned\n- New tasks start with `status: 'pending'`\n- When dequeued, task status changes to `'processing'`\n- `dequeue()` returns `null` when the queue is empty\n\n## Export\n\nExport the `TaskQueue` class as a named export from `src/index.ts`.\n# Phase 2: Named Queues\n\nExtend the `TaskQueue` to support multiple named queues.\n\n## Updated Methods\n\n- **`enqueue(queueName, payload)`** - Add a task to a specific named queue. Returns the created task.\n- **`dequeue(queueName)`** - Get the next task from a specific named queue. Returns `null` if queue is empty or doesn't exist.\n- **`list